From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 02:25:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: do not advertise unsupported EHT MAC capabilities

The driver capabilities include EPCS priority access and Restricted TWT,
but hostapd does not currently implement either feature for an AP. In
particular, the EPCS action frame handling is still explicitly left as a
TODO in ap_drv_ops.c.

Do not copy these hardware capabilities into management frames until the
corresponding hostapd functionality is available. Advertising unsupported
EHT MAC features can make strict stations reject the complete EHT
Capabilities element and associate as HE instead.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
@@ -138,5 +138,8 @@ u8 * hostapd_eid_eht_capab(struct hostap
 	os_memset(cap, 0, sizeof(*cap));
 	cap->mac_cap = host_to_le16(eht_cap->mac_cap);
+	cap->mac_cap &= host_to_le16(~(EHT_MACCAP_EPCS_PRIO |
+					 EHT_MACCAP_RESTRICTED_TWT));
+
 	os_memcpy(cap->phy_cap, eht_cap->phy_cap, EHT_PHY_CAPAB_LEN);
 
 	/* Bits 2-7 of the last EHT PHY capability octet are reserved. */
